window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>Are you into spicy romance tangled with cursed objects? Characters who make bad decisions they can’t take back? Secret societies and magic that demand sacrifice? That’s <i>Crystal Iris</i>.</p> <p>Imagine dark, mystical academia colliding with the grit of a modern western. A whiskey glass full of longing. A black horse under a full moon. A silk dress stained in blood—and cufflinks slipping from a cowboy’s hand.</p> <p>This is the story of Iris De Loughery. Thirty. Engaged. Harvard professor. Perfectly put together—until she inherits a prism necklace she can’t remove. Until it connects her to a man she should never want.</p> <p>Hoyt Locklear. Wealthy. Cursed. With a prism of his own. And completely out of reach. Because every time she touches him, the magic burns him alive. And still, he says—try again.</p> <p>Now she's spiraling. Because the closer they fall, the more the prism pulls—toward mirrors, secrets, and blood.</p> <p>And this is only the beginning. Seven prisms lie hidden across the world. Each with power. Each with a price.</p> <p>“I should run. Instead, I reach for him.”</p>"; 
